23: --     locks the key row (creating it when absent) and, in that transaction,
24: --     returns 'superseded' when generation < fence_generation (nothing is
25: --     written); otherwise raises fence_generation to the given generation and
26: --     returns 'stored' + message_id when the key's message is committed,
27: --     'stored' with a null message_id when a message committed under the key
28: --     through this function was deleted since (so a client never resends a
29: --     message its sender deleted), else 'not_stored'. It never creates a
30: --     message. The create route calls it
