14: /**
15:  * POST /api/messages/fence â€” Phase 5 T2 (FR-006, FR-011, FR-034, BR-001,
16:  * BR-005; SPEC section 12): fence/lookup of the CALLER'S OWN composition key.
17:  * Body: { conversationId, clientMessageId, attemptGeneration, expectedSenderId }
18:  * (all required). The key is always scoped to the authenticated sender
19:  * (users.id resolved from the session), so another user's key is never read
20:  * or changed: it is simply a different (empty) key of the caller.
21:  *
22:  * 200 { outcome: 'stored', clientMessageId, attemptGeneration, message } â€” the
23:  *     key's message is committed (the item resolves as delivered); `message`
24:  *     is null when it was committed and has been deleted since;
25:  * 200 { outcome: 'not_stored', clientMessageId, attemptGeneration } â€” nothing
26:  *     is stored and no attempt older than attemptGeneration can commit any more;
27:  * 409 ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED â€” a newer generation exists (nothing changed);
28:  * 403 SENDER_MISMATCH (expectedSenderId is not the authenticated user; nothing
29:  *     fenced), 403 NOT_PARTICIPANT (incl. a missing conversation), 401 when not
30:  *     signed in, 400 for malformed fields, 429 when rate limited.
31:  * Never creates a message.
32:  */
