54: ## T4 â€” Server-validated atomic mentions and current-member roster
55: Reasoning: Mentions are a data contract consumed by composer and notifications on both create paths; the 
autocomplete needs a current roster no existing read provides.
56: Task: A mention store holds application user IDs mentioned by a message, written in the same transaction as the 
first creation on both the text path and the attachment/voice path, only for conversation members at that time other 
than the sender; requested mention IDs are part of the stored original composition (changed mentions on replay â†’ 
409; unchanged replay after a recipient left returns the stored message); only members can read mention records; no 
client can write them; messages fetched by members carry their mention IDs. An authorized read returns a 
conversation's current members (from `conversation_members`, so removed members are excluded) to members only.
57: Done when: The AC-024 server clauses, the AC-046 replay clause, and the roster contract hold on the local database 
for both create paths.
